00:01:08.527 --> 00:01:10.489
- Be the hero of your own movie.

00:01:10.489 --> 00:01:14.007
If your life was a movie
and it started now,

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:16.637
forget about whatever
financial disasters you've had,

00:01:16.637 --> 00:01:19.103
personal failures, relationship failures,

00:01:19.103 --> 00:01:22.357
what would the hero of your life's movie

00:01:22.357 --> 00:01:25.874
do right now, do that, do those things.

00:01:25.874 --> 00:01:30.378
We define ourselves far too
often by our past failures.

00:01:30.378 --> 00:01:32.430
We look at our past and
we say, well, that's me.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:35.186
That's not you, you are
this person right now.

00:01:35.186 --> 00:01:37.612
You're the person who's
learned from those failures

00:01:37.612 --> 00:01:40.662
and you can choose to be
the hero of your own movie

00:01:40.662 --> 00:01:42.677
right now, write down your goals.

00:01:42.677 --> 00:01:44.309
Write down things you want to improve.

00:01:44.309 --> 00:01:46.479
Write down things you won't
tolerate from yourself.

00:01:46.479 --> 00:01:48.863
Write down things that
you've done in the past

00:01:48.863 --> 00:01:52.749
that you never want to see
yourself do again and go forth

00:01:52.749 --> 00:01:55.547
from here as the hero of your own movie.

00:01:55.547 --> 00:01:59.313
Build momentum, build
confidence and momentum with

00:01:59.313 --> 00:02:02.490
each good decision that
you make from here on out.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.370
You can do it, anyone can do it.

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:07.290
We live in unique times, we
live in one of the rarest

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:09.342
times in human history where
you can choose almost all

00:02:09.342 --> 00:02:12.266
of the input that comes your
way, whether its the movies

00:02:12.266 --> 00:02:14.812
that you watch, the books you
read, the podcasts you listen

00:02:14.812 --> 00:02:19.501
to, you can choose to be
inspired, do that, do that.

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:22.849
And be the hero of your own movie.

00:02:22.849 --> 00:02:24.395
It's good to treat other
people the way you would

00:02:24.395 --> 00:02:25.817
like to be treated yourself.

00:02:25.817 --> 00:02:28.119
It's like a golden rule and
there's a reason for it.

00:02:28.119 --> 00:02:30.087
And that reason is that
we're connected in some

00:02:30.087 --> 00:02:32.593
strange way that we
don't totally understand.

00:02:32.593 --> 00:02:34.808
And unless you are good to
other people around you,

00:02:34.808 --> 00:02:37.938
unless you're a kind and
friendly and warm and loving,

00:02:37.938 --> 00:02:40.286
you're not going to enjoy
this life, you're just not.

00:02:40.286 --> 00:02:42.842
You're going to be
problems everywhere you go.

00:02:42.842 --> 00:02:44.892
You're going to have
problems everywhere you go.

00:02:44.892 --> 00:02:47.486
You got to figure out a
way to enjoy this life.

00:02:47.486 --> 00:02:50.712
It's not because of Jesus,
it's not because of Moses.

00:02:50.712 --> 00:02:52.722
It's not because of anybody
that may or may not have

00:02:52.722 --> 00:02:54.811
ever existed, it's
because that's how you fit

00:02:54.811 --> 00:02:57.611
in better in the world,
that's how you stay positive.

00:02:57.611 --> 00:03:00.833
And it doesn't have to be
some that written 5,000 years

00:03:00.833 --> 00:03:03.299
ago on animal skins, that
doesn't have to be the golden

00:03:03.299 --> 00:03:06.177
rule because it's old, that's dumb.

00:03:06.177 --> 00:03:09.351
We need to figure out
like now, today what is,

00:03:09.351 --> 00:03:11.362
the best way to live your life, what is.

00:03:11.362 --> 00:03:15.304
There's got to be ways
you could be putting forth

00:03:15.304 --> 00:03:16.684
the most positive energy, I mean.

00:03:16.684 --> 00:03:19.620
We know objectively
what's causing pollution.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.298
We know objectively what's
causing birth defects

00:03:22.298 --> 00:03:25.350
and we're taking in too much
chemicals and not enough

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.611
vitamins, we know
objectively all this stuff.

00:03:27.611 --> 00:03:30.701
We know how to organize our
world and yet we don't do it.

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:32.039
We know how to organize our health

00:03:32.039 --> 00:03:35.097
and yet very few people do
it, we know all these things.

00:03:35.097 --> 00:03:39.483
The right path to being
a happy, healthy person

00:03:39.483 --> 00:03:41.991
is to do all the that we already
know you're supposed to do.

00:03:41.991 --> 00:03:44.657
Take care of your body,
take care of your health.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.916
Take care of your mind,
your stress, meditate,

00:03:46.916 --> 00:03:48.840
be kind to people, we all know that.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.472
I mean, you ask anybody,
they know how to get by

00:03:50.472 --> 00:03:54.898
and to be the most evolved
version of you that you can be.

00:03:54.898 --> 00:03:57.156
It's not like a magical checklist.

00:03:57.156 --> 00:03:58.658
If you talk to people
about it and you said,

00:03:58.658 --> 00:04:00.992
okay, you got a person,
you want to improve them.

00:04:00.992 --> 00:04:02.745
What are the things that
you're going to do to 'em?

00:04:02.745 --> 00:04:05.009
Okay, well if I was a life
coach, the first thing I would

00:04:05.009 --> 00:04:06.050
say is this guy's got to get

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.599
on a diet that makes him healthy.

00:04:07.599 --> 00:04:08.851
I don't mean a diet just to lose weight.

00:04:08.851 --> 00:04:10.857
I mean just healthy foods in your body,

00:04:10.857 --> 00:04:15.024
many, many vegetables,
vegetables, a lot of good, good

00:04:16.065 --> 00:04:20.168
quality protein, a lot
of water, stop the sodas,

00:04:20.168 --> 00:04:23.216
stop the bull, start
workin' out your body.

00:04:23.216 --> 00:04:25.432
And get a better sense
of like how this machine

00:04:25.432 --> 00:04:29.022
feels when it's moving,
it's flowing better.

00:04:29.022 --> 00:04:31.740
There's less tension in it,
your mind feels like relaxed

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:35.088
and you enjoy every single
moment of the day better.

00:04:35.088 --> 00:04:37.311
Step one, everybody
knows that step, right?

00:04:37.311 --> 00:04:39.021
What's step two, be cool to people.

00:04:39.021 --> 00:04:40.237
Be nice to as many people as you can.

00:04:40.237 --> 00:04:41.873
Smile at as many people as you can.

00:04:41.873 --> 00:04:44.037
Have them smile back at
you, tip well when you go to

00:04:44.037 --> 00:04:46.215
restaurants, just do the most you can.

00:04:46.215 --> 00:04:50.055
Be as nice as you can and
just still manage to not

00:04:50.055 --> 00:04:51.269
have people walk all over you.

00:04:51.269 --> 00:04:53.109
Just get through this
life as nice as you can.

00:04:53.109 --> 00:04:55.113
What else, do what you
want to do with your life.

00:04:55.113 --> 00:04:57.288
Don't be doing something you don't enjoy.

00:04:57.288 --> 00:04:59.416
Don't do something that's,
don't get locked into

00:04:59.416 --> 00:05:02.168
a car that you can't afford
and doing something crazy

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:04.340
because you need the money, don't do that.

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:06.932
Do what you want to do, do
what the is it that you really

00:05:06.932 --> 00:05:10.712
want to do, 'cause if someone
else is doin' it, you can do it.

00:05:10.712 --> 00:05:14.013
Everybody makes their own
path through this world

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:17.155
but a lot of people don't
follow the path that

00:05:17.155 --> 00:05:20.539
they really feel pulled to, ya know.

00:05:20.539 --> 00:05:22.843
'Cause for whatever reason
they got negative programming.

00:05:22.843 --> 00:05:25.431
When they were kids, someone
told 'em they couldn't do it

00:05:25.431 --> 00:05:29.776
or told them to take the
shortcut or take the sure route.

00:05:29.776 --> 00:05:32.204
That's a sad thing, man,
when you talk to dudes,

00:05:32.204 --> 00:05:34.298
especially like talented
dudes and they don't follow up

00:05:34.298 --> 00:05:35.680
with what they want to do, ya know.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:38.316
There's a bunch of people
that will say, yeah,

00:05:38.316 --> 00:05:40.994
well I have a family so
it's all great idea for you

00:05:40.994 --> 00:05:42.708
to just go out there and go crazy.

00:05:42.708 --> 00:05:45.722
I have people to support,
you need to listen.

00:05:45.722 --> 00:05:48.317
Stop sayin' that, stop
sayin' any of those things.

00:05:48.317 --> 00:05:52.119
Every single person who
has ever done anything

00:05:52.119 --> 00:05:56.286
worthwhile or exceptional or
difficult or extraordinary,

00:05:58.093 --> 00:06:01.815
anyone, whether it's
great artists or authors

00:06:01.815 --> 00:06:05.898
or mathematicians or
whatever the it is, everyone

00:06:06.746 --> 00:06:10.382
encounters difficulties,
there is no easy road.

00:06:10.382 --> 00:06:14.549
It does not exist, it is
impossible, everyone has issues.

00:06:15.558 --> 00:06:18.856
If you have time to pursue
a hobby, if you have time

00:06:18.856 --> 00:06:21.700
to do anything in your life,
you can better yourself.

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:24.711
And here's one way you
never better yourself,

00:06:24.711 --> 00:06:27.267
when you come up with
excuses for why other people

00:06:27.267 --> 00:06:30.529
are successful and you're
not, that is dangerous.

00:06:30.529 --> 00:06:33.873
When you give yourself an escape.

00:06:33.873 --> 00:06:34.878
Well, that's easy for you to say, ya know

00:06:34.878 --> 00:06:36.928
you do this or do do do do do, trust me.

00:06:36.928 --> 00:06:40.344
Everybody has a hard
road, I wanted to jump out

00:06:40.344 --> 00:06:42.855
a window several times
during my young life.

00:06:42.855 --> 00:06:45.739
I wanted to jump in front
of a train, just end it

00:06:45.739 --> 00:06:48.119
because it's just too
much pressure, not really.

00:06:48.119 --> 00:06:50.713
But you know what I'm
sayin', theoretically.

00:06:50.713 --> 00:06:53.053
We all go through hard times,
we all go through depression.

00:06:53.053 --> 00:06:57.281
We all go through doubt and
moments in your life where

00:06:57.281 --> 00:06:59.910
it's really difficult and
you're trying to figure

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:04.168
what the your path is
going to be, it's hard as.

00:07:04.168 --> 00:07:06.262
But Steph and I, we were
talking about this before

00:07:06.262 --> 00:07:09.266
the podcast starts that that
is what makes you a person.

00:07:09.266 --> 00:07:12.400
And those difficult moments
are what build your character.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:15.916
Show me a great man who's
the son of a great man.

00:07:15.916 --> 00:07:17.959
That's what we were saying,
these kids that are born

00:07:17.959 --> 00:07:22.433
billionaires, you're,
you're, you're never going

00:07:22.433 --> 00:07:26.709
to be a self made person,
you have a back up trust

00:07:26.709 --> 00:07:30.849
for your back up trust for
your trust, and you're man.

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:34.317
I'm fascinated by Marshall
Arts, I'm fascinated by comedy.

00:07:34.317 --> 00:07:37.330
I'm fascinated by many,
many different things.

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:39.960
I don't understand when
people say they're bored.

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:43.306
Because if I had the
time to live 100 lives,

00:07:43.306 --> 00:07:44.900
I'd be speaking different languages.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.198
I'd be living in different countries.

00:07:46.198 --> 00:07:48.706
I would try a number of different careers.

00:07:48.706 --> 00:07:51.416
'Cause I think there's a lot
of unbelievable fascinating,

00:07:51.416 --> 00:07:55.359
puzzling, complex things that
you could study in this world.

00:07:55.359 --> 00:07:57.411
But that's just me and my
personality but that's the

00:07:57.411 --> 00:07:59.163
personality also that I've cultivated

00:07:59.163 --> 00:08:00.331
over the years of challenges.

00:08:00.331 --> 00:08:01.711
- [Interviewer] Were you
like that as a kid too?

00:08:01.711 --> 00:08:03.631
- Well, I was involved in
Marshall Arts very early.

00:08:03.631 --> 00:08:06.687
And I think that is one of
the things that motivated

00:08:06.687 --> 00:08:11.454
me to explore difficult tasks
because through difficult

00:08:11.454 --> 00:08:14.418
tasks, you learn an incredible
amount about yourself.

00:08:14.418 --> 00:08:18.468
And you, through the
fire of competition, you

00:08:18.468 --> 00:08:22.562
get to understand, you get
to understand motivation.

00:08:22.562 --> 00:08:24.862
You get to understand the
resistance that you have

00:08:24.862 --> 00:08:26.862
inside your mind to doing hard work.

00:08:26.862 --> 00:08:29.455
You get to understand the
rewards of discipline.

00:08:29.455 --> 00:08:32.963
Like you don't truly appreciate
relaxation unless you've

00:08:32.963 --> 00:08:35.931
worked hard and that is the
ying and the yang of life.

00:08:35.931 --> 00:08:40.571
And I've said this to the
point of people getting sick

00:08:40.571 --> 00:08:44.249
of it but one of the worst
decisions a man can make,

00:08:44.249 --> 00:08:48.046
I can only speak for men,
obviously, is to be comfortable.

00:08:48.046 --> 00:08:50.430
I don't think you should
try to be comfortable.

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:53.860
I think what you should try
to do is try to earn comfort.

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:58.070
And if you can get a day
off where you've worked hard

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.616
and you've accomplished goals,

00:08:59.616 --> 00:09:01.286
that day off would be so sweet.

00:09:01.286 --> 00:09:03.087
When I work hard and I
sit in front of the TV,

00:09:03.087 --> 00:09:05.635
I enjoy the out of it, I put my feet up.

00:09:05.635 --> 00:09:08.146
I have a nice drink, I enjoy my free time.

00:09:08.146 --> 00:09:09.149
- [Interviewer] Get one of those chairs

00:09:09.149 --> 00:09:10.149
that kneads your back
or something like that.

00:09:10.149 --> 00:09:11.193
- I do have one of those.
- Do you really?

00:09:11.193 --> 00:09:12.651
- Those are great.
- They're great, right?

00:09:12.651 --> 00:09:14.157
- I don't use it that
much though, honestly.

00:09:14.157 --> 00:09:16.669
I'm more of a workaholic
than I should be, probably.

00:09:16.669 --> 00:09:20.852
If the balance was, I probably
should relax more than I do.

00:09:20.852 --> 00:09:22.234
But I never feel like I earned it.

00:09:22.234 --> 00:09:24.656
But that's part of the reason
whey when I do feel like

00:09:24.656 --> 00:09:26.452
I earned it, I can enjoy it.

00:09:26.452 --> 00:09:31.346
It's 'cause I am more connected
to the idea that I need

00:09:31.346 --> 00:09:35.513
to accomplish things and it's
not like for anybody else's

00:09:36.908 --> 00:09:39.169
benefit other than my own
or anybody else's approval

00:09:39.169 --> 00:09:42.509
other than my own, I
just, when I have a task,

00:09:42.509 --> 00:09:45.639
whether it's, like today I'm
going to write 1,000 words

00:09:45.639 --> 00:09:47.607
or 2,000 or whatever the number is.

00:09:47.607 --> 00:09:50.331
If I don't do that, I'm
not, I write things down.

00:09:50.331 --> 00:09:51.707
Like I'll write down a
list of things to get

00:09:51.707 --> 00:09:54.175
accomplished that day and
if I don't accomplish that,

00:09:54.175 --> 00:09:57.109
I'll get sick, like it'll drive me crazy.

00:09:57.109 --> 00:10:00.328
If I can't fill out that
list, that drives me nuts.

00:10:00.328 --> 00:10:04.308
But that's what led me to
be a championship level

00:10:04.308 --> 00:10:07.576
Marshall Artist, that's
what led me to achieve the,

00:10:07.576 --> 00:10:12.307
it's like that, it's the
reinforcement of those goals.

00:10:12.307 --> 00:10:15.149
Like understanding that you
can achieve those goals.

00:10:15.149 --> 00:10:16.899
It's going to be difficult,
you're going to push through

00:10:16.899 --> 00:10:18.663
the difficulty and then you're
going to understand what

00:10:18.663 --> 00:10:21.379
difficulty truly is and how
much of it is just mental,

00:10:21.379 --> 00:10:22.927
how much of it is just in your mind.

00:10:22.927 --> 00:10:26.844
This adversity to difficult
task or to struggle

00:10:28.115 --> 00:10:30.376
and a lot of people have
that, they're scared.

00:10:30.376 --> 00:10:34.590
They're scared of complications,
they're scared of failure.

00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:36.424
Failure's a big one that
people are afraid of

00:10:36.424 --> 00:10:38.100
but failure is one of the
most important things you

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:39.646
could ever have as far as like

00:10:39.646 --> 00:10:41.736
the motivation to do things differently.

00:10:41.736 --> 00:10:45.903
One of the reasons why I think
that I'm good at friendships

00:10:46.804 --> 00:10:48.523
and relationships is because

00:10:48.523 --> 00:10:50.065
I've failed at them in the past.

00:10:50.065 --> 00:10:51.447
One of things that I'm good at, comedy,

00:10:51.447 --> 00:10:53.497
is because I bombed on stage.

00:10:53.497 --> 00:10:56.051
One of the reasons why I'm
good at work is because

00:10:56.051 --> 00:10:59.351
I've been a worker in the
past and I know the feeling

00:10:59.351 --> 00:11:04.078
of failure, the feeling of
shame of being like a weak

00:11:04.078 --> 00:11:07.554
non motivated, lazy person,
it's a weak feeling.

00:11:07.554 --> 00:11:10.902
You don't respect yourself
and I have this phrase

00:11:10.902 --> 00:11:13.284
that I use all the time to
people to try to motivate

00:11:13.284 --> 00:11:16.796
people, I say that, be the
hero in your own movie.

00:11:16.796 --> 00:11:18.762
Pretend that if your life
was a movie and your life

00:11:18.762 --> 00:11:20.896
started now, what would the hero do?

00:11:20.896 --> 00:11:22.277
What would the person that you respect do?

00:11:22.277 --> 00:11:23.701
What would the person that you admire,

00:11:23.701 --> 00:11:25.545
the person that inspires
you, what would they do.

00:11:25.545 --> 00:11:29.011
Well, do that and if you
do that, you slowly build

00:11:29.011 --> 00:11:32.269
momentum, you like, today
I did what I wanted to do.

00:11:32.269 --> 00:11:35.613
Today I started a class
in Yoga, I did this.

00:11:35.613 --> 00:11:37.537
I did all these things I was
saying I wasn't going to do.

00:11:37.537 --> 00:11:40.804
And now I feel momentum and
momentum is a very important

00:11:40.804 --> 00:11:44.030
point in people's lives,
that's why some folks don't

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:45.908
like to take days off because
they feel like they're

00:11:45.908 --> 00:11:47.836
losing momentum and they
sort of have to restart the

00:11:47.836 --> 00:11:51.098
wheel up again after a vacation.

00:11:51.098 --> 00:11:52.852
And there's a lot of folks that live life

00:11:52.852 --> 00:11:54.318
on a cushy cloud of marshmallows and bull

00:11:54.318 --> 00:11:57.289
and then one day something
goes wrong and I mean,

00:11:57.289 --> 00:12:00.009
that's why spoiled kids are so sad.

00:12:00.009 --> 00:12:02.975
Like a spoiled young boy is
one of the saddest things ever.

00:12:02.975 --> 00:12:05.475
A young boy that becomes a
man and can't take care of

00:12:05.475 --> 00:12:08.485
himself and his dad has
to keep on rescuing him.

00:12:08.485 --> 00:12:11.075
His dad has to keep on
bailing him out of situations

00:12:11.075 --> 00:12:13.041
and giving him money,
I've met guys like that.

00:12:13.041 --> 00:12:15.928
And that is a crippling
affliction when they don't have

00:12:15.928 --> 00:12:18.684
the character themselves to
be able to get by in life.

00:12:18.684 --> 00:12:22.074
They constantly need someone
to help them and bail them out.

00:12:22.074 --> 00:12:25.338
Even as a grown man, I've
met guys in their 40s that

00:12:25.338 --> 00:12:27.682
