00:16:59.173 --> 00:17:00.595
But that's why he's Bill Burr.

00:17:00.595 --> 00:17:02.097
That's why he's really good.

00:17:02.097 --> 00:17:03.971
When you're alone with your thoughts,

00:17:03.971 --> 00:17:06.139
you get an idea of what
your thoughts actually are.

00:17:06.139 --> 00:17:08.145
If you live your life
just acting constantly on

00:17:08.145 --> 00:17:10.986
the momentum of other
people's expectations,

00:17:10.986 --> 00:17:13.286
of you wanting to be liked
by these other people,

00:17:13.286 --> 00:17:17.036
you can run into a trap
and you set up a life

00:17:17.882 --> 00:17:20.136
that you didn't really want, you're.

00:17:20.136 --> 00:17:22.394
You're trapped in this
situation where you have

00:17:22.394 --> 00:17:24.984
a mortgage, you have credit card bills.

00:17:24.984 --> 00:17:26.449
You got student loans you have to pay.

00:17:26.449 --> 00:17:28.205
You have a bunch of going
on that you have to continue

00:17:28.205 --> 00:17:31.959
to feed and all that, and
especially if you have a family.

00:17:31.959 --> 00:17:33.969
And you have to feed them, oh my goodness.

00:17:33.969 --> 00:17:35.895
Then you're fully locked in,
you can't take any chances

00:17:35.895 --> 00:17:40.485
whatsoever and often times,
people make the mistake

00:17:40.485 --> 00:17:44.034
of getting stuck and it
is just a tactical mistake

00:17:44.034 --> 00:17:45.958
just like it would be a
mistake if you got stuck

00:17:45.958 --> 00:17:48.672
in a video game, just
like it would be a mistake

00:17:48.672 --> 00:17:50.882
if you followed a map incorrectly

00:17:50.882 --> 00:17:52.432
and you got stuck in the woods.

00:17:52.432 --> 00:17:55.392
Your life is certainly
some sort of a journey.

00:17:55.392 --> 00:17:57.694
It's certainly some sort
of journey and we have to

00:17:57.694 --> 00:17:59.739
all be aware that when
we're making journeys,

00:17:59.739 --> 00:18:02.117
we're not going to always
make the right steps.

00:18:02.117 --> 00:18:03.873
And sometimes you have
to back up and try again

00:18:03.873 --> 00:18:05.963
and if you're in a position
where you can't back up

00:18:05.963 --> 00:18:08.179
and try again, you've trapped yourself.

00:18:08.179 --> 00:18:12.483
And the system will set
out honey pots for people

00:18:12.483 --> 00:18:15.367
to get trapped in, the
system will set out ideas

00:18:15.367 --> 00:18:17.621
of retirement, the ideas
of the golden years,

00:18:17.621 --> 00:18:19.252
providing you benefits, providing

00:18:19.252 --> 00:18:21.424
you a healthy work environment, why?

00:18:21.424 --> 00:18:23.220
Well, because they want
people to work for them.

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:25.650
They don't want people to
realize their own dreams

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:28.290
and escape and that's a pain
in the ass so you got to

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:30.468
hire more people and train them.

00:18:30.468 --> 00:18:32.928
They want to set it up
so that you stick around.

00:18:32.928 --> 00:18:35.023
Stick around in some sort
of an unsatisfying world.

00:18:35.023 --> 00:18:38.031
It's up to you to see
that video game problem,

00:18:38.031 --> 00:18:40.375
to see that issue as
it comes up on the map.

00:18:40.375 --> 00:18:41.923
And no, I think this is a right turn.

00:18:41.923 --> 00:18:45.147
To see all the problems that
could potentially lay in

00:18:45.147 --> 00:18:47.941
front of you and calculate your future.

00:18:47.941 --> 00:18:49.867
And also look around all
the people that didn't do it

00:18:49.867 --> 00:18:51.629
and look at the misery that they're in

00:18:51.629 --> 00:18:53.343
and learn that you don't
want to be like them.

00:18:53.343 --> 00:18:55.976
And then look at the people
that have kind of taken

00:18:55.976 --> 00:18:57.732
chances and navigated their way.

00:18:57.732 --> 00:18:59.150
What did they do differently than you?

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:01.950
What objectivity do they
have that maybe you lack?

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:04.668
What insight into their own
mistakes are they willing

00:19:04.668 --> 00:19:07.632
to delve into that you're
not, that you step back

00:19:07.632 --> 00:19:11.769
and go, I just don't want to
look at myself that closely?

00:19:11.769 --> 00:19:13.565
But the person who's able
to look at themselves the

00:19:13.565 --> 00:19:16.577
closest is going to get
the more rational results.

00:19:16.577 --> 00:19:18.871
One of the things that's
causing this funk that people

00:19:18.871 --> 00:19:22.225
are in is that we're living
our lives, many of us at least

00:19:22.225 --> 00:19:25.579
in these very unfulfilling
ways where you're going to

00:19:25.579 --> 00:19:27.547
this office with artificial light

00:19:27.547 --> 00:19:30.274
and you're doing something you
don't want to do all day long

00:19:30.274 --> 00:19:31.822
and then you get home and you're tired.

00:19:31.822 --> 00:19:33.532
And on top of that, you're
eating, you're eating

00:19:33.532 --> 00:19:36.831
